## Cells of the tubular compartment of the nephron
To promote differentiation of specific nephron cell types from RV stage, day-8 RV-like cells were harvested, plated as single cells at high density on Laminin-521, and stimulated with renal epithelium growth medium (REGM) and different combinations of growth factors to trigger specification. After 6 days of continued culture in REGM (day 14), the cells appeared heterogeneous with several types of epithelial cells (Fig. 4a). Closer analysis at days 4, 6, 8, and 14 revealed the presence of several types of tubular epithelial cells (Fig. 4b). The expression of proximaltubule markers like sub-unit of sodium/potassium ATPase $(\mathrm{Na^{+}/K^{+}}$ -ATPase), ATPBP1, and AQP1 started at day 8 and was sustained until day 14. A higher expression of CUBN, TJP1, and LRP2 at day 8 is noteworthy (Fig. 4b). Occurrence of $\mathrm{{Na^{+}/K^{+}}}$ -ATPase, AQP1 and lotus lectin corroborated a proximal-tubule epithelial cell-like (PTECs) phenotype of these cells (Fig. 4c: A–D). $\mathrm{\AQPl^{+}}$ cells constitute $57\%$ of the tubular epithelial cell mass at day 14. Markers such as sodium chloride co-transporter (NCCT/SLC12A3) and kidney-specific cadherin (CDH16) were expressed in a minor population, revealing the existence of distal epithelial-like cells (Fig. 4c: E, F). PTECs have the ability to absorb sodium provided in the environment due to the presence of transporters such as $\mathrm{{Na^{+}/K^{+}}}$ -ATPase, and this was demonstrated by performing the sodium green assay on day-14 cells (Fig. 4d). The presence of HOXB7, WNT11, and SOX9 expressing cells indicated collecting duct-like identity. Indeed, we identified cells expressing CLDN4, CLDN8, and grainy head-like 2 (GRHL2). A distinctive clear zone of cobblestone-shaped aquaporin 2 $\mathbf{\Pi}(\mathrm{AQP2})^{+}$ cells, together with expression of GRHL2 and Dolichos biflorus (DB) lectin, indicated the presence of collecting duct constituents, i.e., principal-like cells (PC) (Fig. 4c: G–J). The proportion of PTECs $(>55\%)$ was observed to be six times higher than PC $(<10\%)$ (Fig.  4c: D, J). In addition, day-14 T.E.Cs were able to show tubulogenesis when cultured in matrigel and collagen gels similar to proximal-tubule cell lines (Fig. S4).
## Cells of the glomerular compartment of the nephron
Interestingly, when day-8 AB4RA-G-induced RV-like cells were plated at a low density in the presence of hepatocyte growth factor (HGF) in REGM, they acquired an arborized cell body with multiple undivided nuclei indicative of a podocyte-like phenotype. The occurrence of transcription factors like SULF2, MAFB, and MAGI2 at the RNA level presents evidence of the cells being specified to the podocyte lineage. Around $70\%$ of the cells were Podocalyxin (PODXL1) positive, expressing Synaptopodin (SYNPO) and Podocin (NPHS2) (Fig. 5a, b). A down-regulation in WT1 is observed from day 8 to day 14 (Fig. 5c). Further analysis into the regulators of this master transcription factor revealed a decrease in downstream targets like PAX2-8 and a parallel increase in negative regulators PRDM1 and NROB1 and WNT4 within days 8–14 which could attribute to WT-1 down-regulation (Fig. S4). Thus, to improve podocyte differentiation by activating WT-1, an inhibitor of WNT signaling could be used. Functionality of podocytes is demonstrated by the endocytosis of Albumin–FITC (Fig. 5f). Upon 6 days of BMP7/FGF2 treatment, the day-8 RV-like cells obtain a mesangial phenotype expressing alpha smooth actin (ASMA), platelet-derived-growth factor receptor ß (PDGFRB), and DESMIN [27] (Fig. 5d, e). The occurrence of mesangial-like cells indicates the emergence of a stromal population [27, 28] because of the AB4RA-G induction. This is supported by RNA-seq data that indicate the presence of FOXD1 progenitors at days 4 and 8 (data not shown). In summary, we were able to show the derivation of 5 nephronal cell types resembling proximal-, distal-, and collecting tubular epithelial cells, podocyte precursors, and mesangial cells from AB4RA-G-treated cells within 14 days, using novel induction factors.
## Discussion
We have developed a novel chemically defined protocol for the directed differentiation of hPSCs towards the renal lineage (Fig. 6). Broadly, we divide the protocol into three stages starting with the transient enrichment of intermediate mesodermal cell populations known to precede metanephric kidney formation. The initial 4-day exposure to Activin A, BMP4, and Retinoic acid (AB4RA), generating IM, UB, and MM forms the basis for a second step leading to nascent nephronal progenitors of the RV and CSB
