## Pellet culture
The pellet culture was adapted from Takasato 2014 [7]. IMR90-iPS-derived AB4RA-G-induced cells were harvested and dissociated into single cells using Accutase (ThermoFisher Scientific) at days 8–9 of the differentiation. Around $3\ –5\times10\textsuperscript{5}$ cells were spun down a $\mathrm{t}\times400g$ for $5\mathrm{{min}}$ to form a pellet and then placed onto a trans-well filter membrane ${\mathrm{0.4}\upmu\mathrm{m}}$ polyester, Greiner bio-one) on the culture media of $10\%$ FCS/DMEM for 4 days $(n=3)$ ). Following 4 days of culture, the pellet was fixed and stained by immunofluorescence. The samples from this study were imaged using Leica S450 two-photon microscope and Operetta High content imaging system (Perkin Elmer).
## Sodium uptake
To determine the levels of sodium transport in hPSCderived proximal tubular epithelial (PTEC) cells, confluent monolayers of day-14 T.E.Cs were first pre-incubated with $5\times10^{5}\mathrm{M}$ ouabain to inhibit $\mathrm{{Na^{+}/K^{+}}}$ ATPase for $^{\textrm{1h}}$ prior to sodium uptake studies. The cell monolayer was incubated at $37^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $30~\mathrm{{min}}$ in a loading medium (culture medium with $5\times10^{5}\mathrm{M}$ sodium green). At the end of the incubation period, the monolayers were gently washed three times with PBS. A fluorescence spectrum (excitation at $485\mathrm{nm}$ , emission at $535~\mathrm{nm}$ ) of each well was measured using a multiwell plate reader.
## Albumin uptake
For the permeability assay, differentiated hiPSC-derived podocytes (day 14) were cultured as described above, and after differentiation the culture medium was replaced with serum-free media with/without FITC-labeled albumin 1 $\mathrm{0.5\mg/ml}$ ; Abcam) and cultured at $37^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $^{\textrm{1h}}$ , in comparison with control cells cultured at $4~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ . The cells were fixed in $4\%$ paraformaldehyde (PFA) and counterstained with DAPI. Assays were performed in triplicate using separate cell preparations.
## Statistical analysis
All experiments were performed with technical replicates (at least 3). Graphically represented data were subject to statistical analysis for significance such as Kruskal–Wallis test and ANOVA test using the Graphpad prism software. The source data are available on request.
